==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|gmq-pro|hānaʀ|lang=non}}, of uncertain origin. Perhaps a compound of *he- (answering to English {{term|he|lang=en}}) and *ānaʀ (from {{proto|gem-pro|jainaz|lang=non}}, answering to Gothic {{term|𐌾𐌰𐌹𐌽𐍃|tr=jains|lang=got}}) or even directly from *ānaʀ with h- added due to influence from the demonstrative pronoun {{term|hinn|lang=non}}, or else perhaps directly inherited from Proto-Indo-European and answering to {{etyl|grc|-}} {{term|κεῖνος|tr=keînos|lang=grc}}.

===Pronoun===
{{head|non|pronoun}}

# [[he]]

====Descendants====
* Icelandic: {{l|is|hann}}
* Faroese: {{l|fo|hann}}
* Norwegian: {{l|no|han}}
* Danish: {{l|da|han}}
* Swedish: {{l|sv|han}}

